@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+[
+{ type: install
+  message: <<EOM
+SigNoz stores telemetry in ClickHouse (databases/clickhouse), which may
+run on another host. Before the first start, ClickHouse needs a cluster
+named "cluster" and the SigNoz schema. The schema is created by the
+schema migrator of the SigNoz OpenTelemetry Collector, which also
+ingests the telemetry and is packaged separately.
+
+Settings come from built-in defaults, from %%ETCDIR%%/signoz.yaml,
+and from SIGNOZ_* variables set in signoz_env, each overriding the one
+before. A nested key is joined with "_", so
+telemetrystore.clickhouse.dsn is SIGNOZ_TELEMETRYSTORE_CLICKHOUSE_DSN.
+signoz_config may list more YAML files, later ones overriding earlier
+ones. Upstream's reference to every key is installed as
+%%DATADIR%%/example.yaml; its values are examples, not the defaults,
+so do not use it as a configuration.
+
+The alert and email templates are in %%ETCDIR%%/templates and may be
+edited in place.
+
+By default SigNoz listens on all interfaces: the web interface and API
+on port 8080, its Prometheus metrics on port 9090, and pprof on port
+6060. Port 9090 is also the Prometheus default. To keep pprof off the
+network and move the metrics, set for example:
+
+  sysrc signoz_env="SIGNOZ_PPROF_ENABLED=false \
+SIGNOZ_INSTRUMENTATION_METRICS_READERS_PULL_EXPORTER_PROMETHEUS_PORT=9464"
+
+The SQLite metadata store is kept in /var/db/signoz.
+EOM
+}
+]
